#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186343056 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f3bd5e5c-b8d1-53e5-9968-8bef8faceb4b" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Trigonometric Equation Containing the Tangent Function Transformed by Multiple Operations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a9afd5b5-4ca7-5dc7-831d-30f699365815" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343058}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a9afd5b5-4ca7-5dc7-831d-30f699365815" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343058} :answer-field/id #uuid "190cb89e-aebf-5c8e-b23b-575fc6dd86fa" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343057} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "787cc3ad-32ad-5fce-bffc-0e8e8c889a13" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7\\pi}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343060}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "787cc3ad-32ad-5fce-bffc-0e8e8c889a13" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7\\pi}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343060} :answer-field/id #uuid "06c51fb8-b2f0-519d-8688-cf5b5bd5ebb7" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343059} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "65bc3bb5-45cf-58fb-b8aa-5d841b3d2f57" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{13\\pi}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343062}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "65bc3bb5-45cf-58fb-b8aa-5d841b3d2f57" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{13\\pi}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343062} :answer-field/id #uuid "7ea2b303-c0b2-5bab-9afa-861157738687" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343061} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3d6b62da-c982-58b5-8dcf-6c74ac9845ac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{19\\pi}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343064}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3d6b62da-c982-58b5-8dcf-6c74ac9845ac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{19\\pi}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343064} :answer-field/id #uuid "b862c844-7b1d-591f-bef5-a14dd2676b4e" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343063}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "2ccfedc3-8e1d-5dac-9606-34084cd890a2" :question/math-academy-id "q-328350" :question/problem "Expressed in **ascending order** in radians, the **exact solutions** to the equation  $3tan\\,(2x+\\frac{\\pi }{6})-3\\sqrt{3}=0,$ for $0\\le x<2\\pi ,$ are\n\n${x}_{1}=$\n{{field-1}}$,\\,{x}_{2}=$\n{{field-2}}$,\\,{x}_{3}=$\n{{field-3}}$,\\,{x}_{4}=$\n{{field-4}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3\\operatorname{tan}⁡(2x+\\frac{\\pi }{6})-3\\sqrt{3} & =0 \\\\ 3\\operatorname{tan}⁡(2x+\\frac{\\pi }{6}) & =3\\sqrt{3} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡(2x+\\frac{\\pi }{6}) & =\\sqrt{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe will find the general solution to the equation, and then generate all of the solutions in the required domain.\n\nThe general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n2x+\\frac{\\pi }{6}=\\frac{\\pi }{3}+n\\pi .\n$$\n\nSolving the equation above for $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x & =\\frac{\\pi }{3}-\\frac{\\pi }{6}+n\\pi  \\\\ 2x & =\\frac{\\pi }{6}+n\\pi  \\\\ x & =\\frac{\\pi }{12}+\\frac{n\\pi }{2} \\\\ x & =\\frac{(6n+1)\\pi }{12}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe set $n=0,\\pm 1,\\pm 2,…,$ until we have generated all solutions in the domain $0\\le x<2\\pi .$\n\n- Setting $n=0$ gives $x=\\frac{\\pi }{12}$\n\n- Setting $n=1$ gives $x=\\frac{7\\pi }{12}$\n\n- Setting $n=2$ gives $x=\\frac{13\\pi }{12}$\n\n- Setting $n=3$ gives $x=\\frac{19\\pi }{12}$\n\nAll other values of $n$ generate solutions outside the domain $0\\le x<2\\pi .$ \n\nSo, in ascending order, the solutions are \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=\\frac{\\pi }{12},\\,{x}_{2}=\\frac{7\\pi }{12},\\,{x}_{3}=\\frac{13\\pi }{12},\\,{x}_{4}=\\frac{19\\pi }{12}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186343065 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9eb12a99-5169-52f7-8830-5de0d2d854f6" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Trigonometric Equation Containing a Transformed Tangent Function Under a Modified Domain"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1eb68341-b796-5347-a7b8-8e1c6144b5aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-180" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343067}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1eb68341-b796-5347-a7b8-8e1c6144b5aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-180" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343067} :answer-field/id #uuid "bac141b0-1322-5b9e-bf4e-e58b94ef95c9" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343066} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d501dd71-637d-5a79-9da9-43a3412b618f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-90" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343069}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d501dd71-637d-5a79-9da9-43a3412b618f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-90" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343069} :answer-field/id #uuid "5b3c713c-136a-5aca-ae53-2b5eb3571ad8" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343068}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "aa7852c7-812a-5d97-bd66-542840db60ff" :question/math-academy-id "q-328369" :question/problem "Expressed in **ascending order** in degrees, the **exact solutions** to the equation $\\operatorname{tan}⁡(2x+{45}^{∘})=1,$ for $-{180}^{∘}\\le x<0,$  are\n\n${x}_{1}=$\n{{field-1}}${}^{∘},\\,{x}_{2}=$\n{{field-2}}${}^{∘}.$" :question/worked-solution "We will find the general solution to the equation, and then generate all of the solutions in the required domain.\n\nThe general solution to our equation is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x+{45}^{∘} & ={45}^{∘}+n\\cdot {180}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving our equation for $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x & =-{45}^{∘}+{45}^{∘}+n\\cdot {180}^{∘} \\\\ 2x & =n\\cdot {180}^{∘} \\\\ x & =n\\cdot {90}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe set $n=0,\\pm 1,\\pm 2,…,$ until we have generated all solutions in the domain $-{180}^{∘}\\le x<0.$\n\n- Setting $n=-2$ gives $x=-{180}^{∘}$\n\n- Setting $n=-1$ gives $x=-{90}^{∘}$\n\nAll other values of $n$ generate solutions outside the domain $-{180}^{∘}\\le x<0.$ \n\nSo, the solutions to the equation, in ascending order, are \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}={-180}^{∘},\\,{x}_{2}={-90}^{∘}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186343070 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f3bd5e5c-b8d1-53e5-9968-8bef8faceb4b" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Trigonometric Equation Containing the Tangent Function Transformed by Multiple Operations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "803984a4-031c-5a40-820c-8fa963cf49f3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\,265" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343072} {:answer/id #uuid "fb1150d8-fbf5-54ac-8f7c-5d00aa29736a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\,750" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343073} {:answer/id #uuid "f01c2a25-6356-5cf6-8c46-114c3db75ddc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\,005" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343074} {:answer/id #uuid "d5f61731-1626-5143-9f3b-1411cc5557f8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\,526" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343075} {:answer/id #uuid "bf8d4ab6-6044-5b97-af0d-ad2e27cff690" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\,075" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343076}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bf8d4ab6-6044-5b97-af0d-ad2e27cff690" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\,075" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343076} :answer-field/id #uuid "5157c32d-d421-56a1-994d-8a3d81fedcc9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343071}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "ca5d3a4d-d32a-5591-b61b-0726227bd885" :question/math-academy-id "q-82373" :question/problem "Consider the equation $\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(2x-{45}^{∘})-\\sqrt{3}=0$ for ${0}^{∘}\\le x<{360}^{∘}.$ If the exact solutions ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},{x}_{3}$ and ${x}_{4}$ are written in ascending order, what is the numerical value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(2x-{45}^{∘})-\\sqrt{3} & =0 \\\\ \\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(2x-{45}^{∘}) & =\\sqrt{3} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡(2x-{45}^{∘}) & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{\\sqrt{3}} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡(2x-{45}^{∘}) & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe will find the general solution to the equation, and then generate all of the solutions in the required domain.\n\nThe general solution to our equation is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x-{45}^{∘} & ={45}^{∘}+n\\cdot {180}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving our equation for $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x & ={45}^{∘}+{45}^{∘}+n\\cdot {180}^{∘} \\\\ 2x & ={90}^{∘}+n\\cdot {180}^{∘} \\\\ x & ={45}^{∘}+n\\cdot {90}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe set $n=0,\\pm 1,\\pm 2,…,$ until we have generated all solutions in the domain ${0}^{∘}\\le x<{360}^{∘}.$\n\n- Setting $n=0$ gives $x={45}^{∘}$\n\n- Setting $n=1$ gives $x={135}^{∘}$\n\n- Setting $n=2$ gives $x={225}^{∘}$\n\n- Setting $n=3$ gives $x={315}^{∘}$\n\nAll other values of $n$ generate solutions outside the domain ${0}^{∘}\\le x<{360}^{∘}.$ So, the solutions ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},{x}_{3}$ and ${x}_{4}$ (written in ascending order) are\n\n$$\nx={45}^{∘},{135}^{∘},{225}^{∘},{315}^{∘}.\n$$\n\nFinally, the numerical value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}$ is $45\\cdot 135=6\\,075.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186343077 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f3bd5e5c-b8d1-53e5-9968-8bef8faceb4b" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Trigonometric Equation Containing the Tangent Function Transformed by Multiple Operations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a7508151-97d1-52bb-bac2-9bad8852abcb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{85{\\pi }^{2}}{24}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343079} {:answer/id #uuid "33bd5351-db78-5a1d-94ec-cfeffa31ba3b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5{\\pi }^{2}}{24}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343080} {:answer/id #uuid "4df24be7-7040-5495-b853-b92e41afb9e9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{85\\pi }{576}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343081} {:answer/id #uuid "21693bd1-8502-56ad-a254-0db26b8ff31f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{85{\\pi }^{2}}{576}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343082} {:answer/id #uuid "9681b628-9399-5a9f-8b7f-8b6a234949fc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{17{\\pi }^{2}}{576}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343083}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "21693bd1-8502-56ad-a254-0db26b8ff31f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{85{\\pi }^{2}}{576}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343082} :answer-field/id #uuid "e2a71cf1-f245-5ce1-94e5-a1187e76e035" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343078}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c4570ce6-8681-560b-93a0-ff873c068a50" :question/math-academy-id "q-8479" :question/problem "Consider the equation $\\operatorname{tan}⁡(2x-\\frac{\\pi }{4})=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}$ for $0\\le x<2\\pi .$ Given that the exact solutions ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},{x}_{3}$ and ${x}_{4}$ are written in ascending order, what is the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "We will find the general solution to the equation, and then generate all of the solutions in the required domain.\n\nThe general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x-\\frac{\\pi }{4} & =\\frac{\\pi }{6}+n\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the equation above for $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x & =\\frac{\\pi }{4}+\\frac{\\pi }{6}+n\\pi  \\\\ 2x & =\\frac{5\\pi }{12}+n\\pi  \\\\ x & =\\frac{n\\pi }{2}+\\frac{5\\pi }{24}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe set $n=0,\\pm 1,\\pm 2,…,$ until we have generated all solutions in the domain $0\\le x<2\\pi .$\n\n- Setting $n=0$ gives $x=\\frac{5\\pi }{24}$\n\n- Setting $n=1$ gives $x=\\frac{17\\pi }{24}$\n\n- Setting $n=2$ gives $x=\\frac{29\\pi }{24}$\n\n- Setting $n=3$ gives $x=\\frac{41\\pi }{24}$\n\nAll other values of $n$ generate solutions outside the domain $0\\le x<2\\pi .$ So, the solutions ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},{x}_{3},{x}_{4}$ (written in ascending order) are\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{5\\pi }{24},\\frac{17\\pi }{24},\\frac{29\\pi }{24},\\frac{41\\pi }{24}.\n$$\n\nFinally, since ${x}_{1}=\\frac{5\\pi }{24}$ and ${x}_{2}=\\frac{17\\pi }{24},$ we have\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}=\\frac{5\\pi }{24}\\cdot \\frac{17\\pi }{24}=\\frac{85{\\pi }^{2}}{576}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186343084 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9eb12a99-5169-52f7-8830-5de0d2d854f6" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Trigonometric Equation Containing a Transformed Tangent Function Under a Modified Domain"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3d612ae0-6b0e-5a1f-af24-a1113e212283" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{13\\pi }{576}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343086} {:answer/id #uuid "690e7bf6-e386-59a3-825b-a2c7d3b899c5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{13{\\pi }^{2}}{576}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343087} {:answer/id #uuid "d56d1bc8-98f4-5684-962d-6fff8e046866" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{13{\\pi }^{2}}{576}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343088} {:answer/id #uuid "498bf143-4564-53e5-85eb-b32de2c5b41a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{13{\\pi }^{2}}{24}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343089} {:answer/id #uuid "da4af912-afaa-51c5-8bb6-1232477cf03b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{13\\pi }{24}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343090}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d56d1bc8-98f4-5684-962d-6fff8e046866" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{13{\\pi }^{2}}{576}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343088} :answer-field/id #uuid "497c3159-d911-5616-9754-02dbc7702710" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343085}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3eb110db-f4a7-568d-994f-26f7cca1ce4e" :question/math-academy-id "q-8557" :question/problem "Given that ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are the exact solutions to the equation $\\operatorname{tan}⁡(2x-\\frac{11\\pi }{6})=1$ for $0\\le x<\\pi ,$ what is the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "We will find the general solution to the equation, and then generate all of the solutions in the required domain.\n\nThe general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x-\\frac{11\\pi }{6} & =\\frac{\\pi }{4}+n\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the equation above for $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x & =\\frac{11\\pi }{6}+\\frac{\\pi }{4}+n\\pi  \\\\ 2x & =\\frac{25\\pi }{12}+n\\pi  \\\\ x & =\\frac{25\\pi }{24}+\\frac{n\\pi }{2} \\\\ x & =\\frac{(12n+25)\\pi }{24}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe set $n=0,\\pm 1,\\pm 2,…,$ until we have generated all solutions in the domain $0\\le x<\\pi .$\n\n- Setting $n=-2$ gives $x=\\frac{\\pi }{24}$\n\n- Setting $n=-1$ gives $x=\\frac{13\\pi }{24}$\n\nAll other values of $n$ generate solutions outside the domain $0\\le x<\\pi .$ So, the solutions are $x=\\frac{\\pi }{24},\\frac{13\\pi }{24}.$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}=\\frac{\\pi }{24}\\cdot \\frac{13\\pi }{24}=\\frac{13{\\pi }^{2}}{576}.\n$$"}]}
